hey it's alex and today i'm going to  show you how to make my chicken cordon  bleu bake  [Music]  cold on blue so this recipe is kind of a  cross between a classic chicken cordon  bleu  and a beef wellington so i have the  classic elements of a chicken cordon  bleu but instead of the breading outside  i did a pastry outside so the chicken  cordon bleu inside is all very classic  and traditional so you can choose to  season your breasts individually but i  just threw them on the bowl and seasoned  that all in there just to make it a  little easier and faster so you're going  to want to pound out your chicken breast  until it's pretty thin this will help  you to roll it in the next step if you  happen to have a metal mallet that's a  really easy way to make sure your  chicken is pounded out properly but  there's other tools you can use flying  around in your house to make sure you  get that thin piece of chicken i use a  wooden spoon it takes a little extra  effort but it still works and you could  also use a cast iron skillet so i  layered this with a double layer of the  cheese  just to make sure you get that extra  ooey gooey cheesy center and actually  made for a pretty good visual at the end  [Music]  so to make the rolling process easier i  hung my chicken on a piece of plastic  wrap so once you roll it up you're able  to encase that in the plastic and roll  it even tighter you want a really tight  seal so rolling it back and forth will  help you achieve that you kind of want  to get all the air you can out of it and  tightly roll it and seal it on the edges  so they have a nice  tight  little chicken  well chicken they look like little like  piggies  so putting the chicken back in the  fridge is an important step to allow the  chicken to kind of firm up and hold its  shape so now for the outside i used puff  pastry because that is classic to a beef  wellington i trim the puffed pastry down  just because with the individual wrapped  chickens you don't want to have too much  extra puff pastry  because it'll just be like too bready  and also it might not cook like all the  way through if there's a lot of extra  kind of bunched up right there so  classically in a wellington the puff  pastry is brushed with english mustard  you could really use any like mustard  variety that you like like a dijon or  just a regular yellow mustard but  english mustard has a ton of flavor and  a really bright vibrant yellow color and  you can usually find it at most grocery  stores so once your chickens are cooled  and set pop that right on the puff  pastry and give it a wrap now again if  you have too much extra puff pastry trim  that off and then you can tuck the sides  under and kind of fix it so it looks  really nice  the egg wash will help your puff pastry  get really nice and brown and golden  color once it's baked so then it's time  to get a little fancy with it so in  order to create a nice design on the  outside i took a fork and kind of drew  marks in the puff pastry itself so i did  the lines one way and then i went back  and did it diagonally so it had a nice  kind of diamond pattern on the puff  pastry so once it baked it looks really  nice and pretty then hit it with a  little more salt  and you're ready to bake salt bae that  ish  so you want to bake your rolls until of  course the chicken is cooked through now  this chicken will actually cook pretty  fast because it's pounded out so thin so  it just won't take as long to cook as  like a full piece of chicken breast  but you also are looking for a really  deep golden brown color on the puff  pastry to make sure it's all the way  cooked through pounding out the chicken  breasts and rolling it up like this will  help you get that really beautiful  spiral center that every chicken corn on  blue should have also what's great about  using the puff pastry as opposed to a  classic chicken cordon bleu breading is  that it's so much cleaner breading is  often pretty messy since you have like a  lot going on with the egg and the bread  crumbs and the flour  but this you get it all in one go and  no mess no fuss  it's what i like  this dish is also super show stopping  it's a great dish for a dinner party  they're pretty big so you might not need  to eat the whole thing but they look  really fancy and they taste even better  and they're also so cute look at them  they're like little  i don't know what a good word for that i  keep doing this  they're just so cute  [Music]  you
 

